From 75061a913c0c27d5dc40fd62f37a6b8853847756 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LGA1150 <9155358+LGA1150@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 19:48:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: eip93 - avoid partial DMA output words in authenc

Reading authenc tags from saved hash state avoids packet-tag corruption,
but Airoha also corrupts partial final words of the cipher payload. The
direct test reports two incorrect plaintext bytes in SHA224/RFC3686 case
323 despite successful tag verification. Its 16368-byte payload and
63-byte AAD produce 16431 output bytes. The first of the final three bytes
changes from 0x48 to 0xb4, matching the last output byte, while both DMA
buffers already use aligned bounce allocations.

Use the existing synchronous authenc fallback when AAD plus cipher
payload is not a multiple of four. Check the actual output length in both
directions, excluding the received tag on decryption. Passing the exact
original request to the fallback preserves its HMAC and ciphertext;
padding the authenticated input to round the DMA length would not.
Word-multiple requests continue through the hardware path subject to the
existing empty-payload and AAD-offset restrictions.

This conservatively avoids partial packet-output words for authenc and
costs hardware acceleration for those lengths. It does not change DMA
burst settings or establish the underlying hardware/interconnect fault.

Host GCC 14.2 W=1 builds the full module. A QEMU software model with
partial-word byte replication reproduces the reported decrypt mismatch
before the guard. Afterward, the existing test module passes all 12824
authenc cases, with 14436 modeled async operations and no partial output
word reaching the model. Physical EIP93 confirmation is still needed.

Signed-off-by: LGA1150 <9155358+LGA1150@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 eip93-aead.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/eip93-aead.c b/eip93-aead.c
index fdc9ace..b1978c6 100644
--- a/eip93-aead.c
+++ b/eip93-aead.c
@@ -244,6 +244,10 @@ static bool eip93_aead_needs_fallback(struct aead_request *req,
 	if (!textsize)
 		return true;
 
+	/* A partial output word can repeat its last byte on Airoha. */
+	if (!IS_ALIGNED(req->assoclen + textsize, sizeof(u32)))
+		return true;
+
 	if (IS_ALIGNED(req->assoclen, sizeof(u32)))
 		return req->assoclen / sizeof(u32) > max_offset;
 
-- 
2.52.0

